21ky|n|An argillaceous rock which readily splits into thin plates; argillite; argillaceous schist. ; Any rock or stone having a slaty structure. ; A prepared piece of such stone. ; A thin, flat piece, for roofing or covering houses, etc. ; A tablet for writing upon. ; An artificial material, resembling slate, and used for the above purposes. ; A thin plate of any material; a flake. ; A list of candidates, prepared for nomination or for election; a list of candidates, or a programme of action, devised beforehand. ; To cover with slate, or with a substance resembling slate; as, to slate a roof; to slate a globe. ; To register (as on a slate and subject to revision), for an appointment. ; To set a dog upon; to bait; to slat. See 2d Slat, 3.	a:8r9,106,18;e8c,100,28~e8c,100,28;8r9,106,18	v:1qz9,51,1~1qz9,51,1	n:11rc,130,13;1qz9,88,13~11rc,130,13;1qz9,88,13
