21p4|a|Not decidedly marked; not forcible; inconsiderable; unimportant; insignificant; not severe; weak; gentle; -- applied in a great variety of circumstances; as, a slight (i. e., feeble) effort; a slight (i. e., perishable) structure; a slight (i. e., not deep) impression; a slight (i. e., not convincing) argument; a slight (i. e., not thorough) examination; slight (i. e., not severe) pain, and the like. ; Not stout or heavy; slender. ; Foolish; silly; weak in intellect.	j:1jz8,89,4;1emo,81,19;2bnz,81,6;m2x,81,4;13mr,79,2;ld1,79,4;2e90,78,18;18n,78,10;1emp,77,19;2e8y,74,19;2blx,72,4;13k3,72,25;ls8,71,50;k10,70,2;ai2,70,6~ls8,71,50;ls6,49,38;cv7,37,36;cul,50,34;cvi,52,34;13k3,72,25;1emp,77,19;2e8y,74,19;1emo,81,19;2e90,78,18;8lu,27,17;1el,50,16;143c,46,14;18n,78,10;1r0b,6,9	e:2epf,26,59;1iph,3,14;s3j,1,11~2epf,26,59;1iph,3,14;s3j,1,11
